cease_desist.template:
CEASE AND DESIST LETTER

CASE REF: {caseNumber}

VIA CERTIFIED MAIL

TO: {opposingParty}
FROM: {ourClient}
DATE: {date}

RE: IMMEDIATE CEASE AND DESIST DEMAND
{matterDescription}


Dear Sir/Madam:

This firm represents {ourClient} in connection with the above-referenced matter. We write to demand that you immediately cease and desist from the conduct described herein.

UNLAWFUL CONDUCT

It has come to our client's attention that you have engaged in the following wrongful conduct:

{matterDescription}

This conduct violates our client's rights and causes ongoing harm.

DEMAND

You are hereby demanded to:

1. Immediately cease and desist from all infringing activity;
2. Confirm in writing within ten (10) days that you have complied with this demand;
3. Preserve all documents and communications related to this matter.

CONSEQUENCES OF NON-COMPLIANCE

If you fail to comply with this demand, our client is prepared to pursue all available legal remedies, including but not limited to:

- Seeking injunctive relief;
- Filing a civil lawsuit for damages;
- Reporting the matter to appropriate authorities.

This letter shall not be construed as a waiver of any rights or remedies available to our client.

Govern yourself accordingly.

Very truly yours,

_______________________
{lawyerName}
{firmName}

settlement_offer.template:
SETTLEMENT OFFER
CONFIDENTIAL - FOR SETTLEMENT PURPOSES ONLY

CASE NO: {caseNumber}

FROM: {ourClient}
TO: {opposingParty}
DATE: {date}

RE: Settlement Offer - {matterDescription}


Without admission of liability, and solely for the purpose of resolving this dispute, {ourClient} hereby extends the following settlement offer:

TERMS

1. Payment: ${amount}
2. Timing: Within thirty (30) days of execution of settlement agreement
3. Release: Mutual general release of all claims
4. Confidentiality: Terms to remain confidential
5. No admission: Settlement not to be construed as admission of liability

CONDITIONS

This offer is:
- Open for acceptance until {expirationDate}
- Subject to execution of a mutually agreeable settlement agreement
- Contingent upon dismissal with prejudice of all pending claims

This communication is made pursuant to applicable rules regarding settlement negotiations and is inadmissible for any purpose other than settlement discussions.

Please advise at your earliest convenience whether your client wishes to accept this offer or to make a counter-proposal.

Very truly yours,

_______________________
{lawyerName}
{firmName}
